.TH KIRO-AUR-CHECK 8 "2026-11-26" "Kiro" "Kiro System Tools"
.SH NAME
kiro-aur-check \- show the lines of an AUR package worth a look before it is built
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiro-aur-check
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fIfolder\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiro-aur-check
reads the PKGBUILD in \fIfolder\fR (default: the current folder) and the scripts next to it
with
.BR cachyos-pi-scan (1)
\- CachyOS Package Installer's scanner \- and prints what deserves a closer look:
downloading and running a script, reading keys, passwords or browser data, unverified
sources, services enabled from an install script, and more. Nothing from the package is
executed. It then adds the package's AUR history: orphaned, maintainer changed, less than
30 days old, very few votes.
.PP
On Kiro, paru runs it before every AUR build through
.B PreBuildCommand
in the
.B [bin]
section of
.IR /etc/paru.conf ,
set by
.BR kiro-paru-aur-check (8).
When a finding is dangerous it asks whether to continue; answering no (or having no
terminal to ask on) exits 1, which stops paru before the build. Warnings and notes are
only shown.
.PP
This is a reading aid, not a guarantee: no findings does not make a package safe.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PKGBASE
Set by paru; the package name used for the AUR history. Without it the name comes from
.I .SRCINFO
or the folder name.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the build may go on, 1 when it should stop (a dangerous finding that was not
confirmed).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/cachyos-pi-scan
The scanner (package cachyos-pi-scan). Without it nothing is checked and the build goes on.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/kiro-common.sh
Shared library.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
kiro-aur-check ~/Downloads/some-package
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kiro-paru-aur-check (8),
.BR paru.conf (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Dubois <https://www.erikdubois.be>
